    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.01) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), our two premier plays of the day. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Mathews, where a +7% platoon boost and prime #2 order placement maximize his ceiling, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leverages a dynamic platoon advantage (R) against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez to secure his spot as a top-tier start. **Jacob Wilson** (74.08) and **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) also present elite options; **Jacob Wilson** is aided by a +10% park factor in his clash with Framber Valdez, and **Cole Carrigg** remains a high-upside play due to the exploitable xERA of Luinder Avila. These starters provide the necessary volume and speed potential to keep our 5x5 totals competitive.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Gunnar Henderson** (53.01) on the bench. Despite his immense talent, his matchup against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez carries significant risk, with a -19% SP skill penalty and a -15% dynamic platoon hit outweighing the +16% park boost. He fell just short of the efficiency required to unseat **Coby Mayo** (49.55), who, despite the tough SP, benefits from favorable wind conditions and a higher overall matchup safety profile. Meanwhile, managers must monitor the 37% rain risk in the games featuring **Drake Baldwin**, **Dominic Smith**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Nasim Nunez**; should these games be delayed or postponed, the efficiency scores for these starters will shift immediately. We remain vigilant, particularly as we rely on **Drake Baldwin** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** for essential production from the top of the lineup.",
